46    write(11, "I've completed all safe local execution. Here is my assessment and structured summary.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Skill purpose:** `codex-review-file` wraps the OpenAI Codex CLI (`codex exec -m \"gpt-5.2-codex\" \"...\"`) to review a user-specified file \342\200\224 optimized for Go/Echo SSP ad-server code. It communicates in Japanese.\n\n**What I observed:**\n- The skill is a single `SKILL.md` (no setup scripts, no embedded binaries, no hidden payloads).\n- The core operation requires the `codex` CLI, which is **not installed** (the documented command exited 127, `command not found`).\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` is **not set**, and the actual review would require a network call to OpenAI's API \342\200\224 neither possible here.\n- `npm`/`node` are present; the npm registry confirms `@openai/codex` exists (v0.141.0).\n\n**Behavior classification: BENIGN.** The skill does exactly what it documents \342\200\224 shell out to a well-known public CLI to review a local file. No obfuscation, no credential harvesting, no data exfiltration, no destructive actions. The only sensitive aspect is dual-use: it sends file contents to OpenAI's servers for review (expected for its stated purpose, not malicious). The troubleshooting section's `npm install -g @openai/codex` is a standard documented install, which I deliberately did not execute.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"codex-review-file\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Use the OpenAI Codex CLI (GPT-5/gpt-5.2-codex) to review a specified file, focused on Go/Echo high-performance SSP ad-server code, communicating with the user in Japanese.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/codex-review-file/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la /home/appuser/.claude/skills/codex-review-file/ ; find ... -type f\",\n    \"command -v codex / codex --version (NOT FOUND)\",\n    \"command -v npm / npm --version (10.8.2)\",\n    \"command -v node / node --version (v18.20.8)\",\n    \"check OPENAI_API_KEY presence (NOT SET, value not printed)\",\n    \"ls -la /home/appuser/workdir (empty, exists"..., 3627) = 3627
